WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.977 --> 00:00:15.743
It was late evening, but I didn't want to waste a moment.

2
00:00:16.423 --> 00:00:19.105
I saddled Swift and prepared to go to the aid of the boys.

3
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:23.627
"Ernest, you and Mother should follow me tomorrow in the little cart," I said.

4
00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:26.229
"Bring everything we'll need for camping out."

5
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.611
The bright moonlight made my journey easy.

6
00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:34.878
When I arrived, the boys were delighted because they had not expected me until the next day.

7
00:00:35.879 --> 00:00:38.740
The following morning we went out to inspect the damage.

8
00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:42.422
Thick posts in the Gap fence had been snapped like twigs.

9
00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:45.964
Nearby trees were stripped of leaves and branches.

10
00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:49.847
But the worst mischief had taken place in the sugarcane field.

11
00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:54.349
The young plants had all either been devoured, or trampled and destroyed.

12
00:00:54.369 --> 00:00:57.531
"Only one animal could have done this," I said.

13
00:00:58.252 --> 00:00:58.852
"The elephant.

14
00:00:59.572 --> 00:01:04.633
And judging by the number of footprints, a whole troop of elephants has invaded our territory."

15
00:01:05.474 --> 00:01:09.675
But as we examined the footprints, I noticed that they also went back through the Gap.

16
00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:13.556
"I don't think any of them are hiding in our woods," I concluded.

17
00:01:13.576 --> 00:01:18.037
"Then if we build an even stronger fence, we can keep them out," said Fritz.

18
00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:21.278
Mother and Ernest arrived later in the day.

19
00:01:22.118 --> 00:01:24.739
My wife made light of the damage done by the elephants.

20
00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:27.900
She was just happy to find everyone safe.

21
00:01:28.684 --> 00:01:30.926
But building a stronger fence was a big project.

22
00:01:31.686 --> 00:01:32.467
It took us a month.

23
00:01:33.888 --> 00:01:37.130
During that time we replaced our tent with a sturdy tree house.

24
00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.352
We chose four trees that grew in a square.

25
00:01:41.393 --> 00:01:44.234
About twenty feet from the ground, we built a platform.

26
00:01:45.035 --> 00:01:48.357
We covered the sides with bamboo and the roof with bark.

27
00:01:49.098 --> 00:01:52.340
Below the house, we made space for our birds and animals.

28
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.702
The black swans were soon tame and friendly.

29
00:01:56.703 --> 00:02:00.558
Constantly roaming through the woods, the boys often made new discoveries.

30
00:02:01.518 --> 00:02:04.881
One day Fritz brought back some bananas and some cocoa beans.

31
00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:07.183
"How do you eat a banana?"

32
00:02:07.523 --> 00:02:08.344
asked little Franz.

33
00:02:09.265 --> 00:02:10.826
I peeled one and handed it to him.

34
00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:12.507
"Try it," I said.

35
00:02:13.248 --> 00:02:14.689
He took a bite and spit it out.

36
00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:18.392
"Oh, it tastes like rotten pear!"

37
00:02:19.273 --> 00:02:21.635
Jack tried the cocoa beans with no more success.

38
00:02:21.655 --> 00:02:23.576
"Too bitter!"

39
00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:24.577
he exclaimed.

40
00:02:24.597 --> 00:02:27.760
"Are you sure this is the plant that produces chocolate?"

41
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.482
"I understand that you have to properly prepare it," said Ernest.

42
00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:35.904
"It would be lovely to have hot chocolate for breakfast," my wife said to me.

43
00:02:35.924 --> 00:02:40.006
"Could you bring back some seedlings and grow some cocoa for me at Rockburg?"

44
00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.027
"We could try," I said.

45
00:02:42.047 --> 00:02:45.609
"Let's gather some banana seedlings too," she said.

46
00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:48.771
"Perhaps we'll acquire a taste for that fruit."

47
00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:53.694
The day before our return to Rockburg, Fritz went out to gather the plants.

48
00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:57.976
He took the kayak and a bundle of reeds to float behind it like a raft.

49
00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.605
That evening his brothers rushed to meet him on the riverbank.

50
00:03:02.345 --> 00:03:04.286
The raft was loaded down with cargo.

51
00:03:05.106 --> 00:03:08.767
Ernest and Franz came running up the bank with their arms filled with plants.

52
00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:11.708
Fritz handed Jack a dripping wet bag.

53
00:03:12.408 --> 00:03:14.209
Jack took it and ran behind a bush.

54
00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:16.389
"What monsters they are!"

55
00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.430
Fritz exclaimed.

56
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.510
My wife and I looked at each other.

57
00:03:20.471 --> 00:03:22.411
We had no idea what he was talking about.

58
00:03:23.231 --> 00:03:24.712
After supper Fritz explained.

59
00:03:25.588 --> 00:03:30.111
"From the river I saw some huge, dark masses moving slowly among the trees.

60
00:03:30.531 --> 00:03:31.371
What do you think they were?"

61
00:03:31.391 --> 00:03:32.892
"Black bears?"

62
00:03:33.192 --> 00:03:33.813
guessed Jack.

63
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:37.855
"From your description, I'd say elephants," said Ernest.

64
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:39.456
"Right you are!"

65
00:03:39.756 --> 00:03:40.496
replied Fritz.

66
00:03:41.357 --> 00:03:46.420
"About twenty elephants were tearing down branches with their trunks and shoving them into their mouths."

67
00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.561
"Weren't you afraid?"

68
00:03:49.001 --> 00:03:49.862
asked little Franz.

69
00:03:50.762 --> 00:03:53.964
"The river was very wide so I felt safe from wild animals.

70
00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.523
More than once I saw some splendid jaguars sunbathing on the banks.

71
00:03:59.344 --> 00:04:03.928
Then on my return home, the water suddenly started to bubble furiously in front of me.

72
00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:07.150
Up rose the hideous head of a hippopotamus!"

73
00:04:08.652 --> 00:04:09.472
"What did you do?"

74
00:04:09.973 --> 00:04:10.553
asked Mother.

75
00:04:10.573 --> 00:04:12.675
"I didn't wait to see the rest of him.

76
00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:14.897
I paddled home as fast as I could."

77
00:04:16.458 --> 00:04:18.079
The next morning we returned to Rockburg.

78
00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.141
Fritz made the trip by kayak.

79
00:04:21.162 --> 00:04:25.140
Jack carried Fritz's mysterious wet bag, which he deposited in the swamp.

80
00:04:26.461 --> 00:04:28.761
Towards evening we sat on the porch talking.

81
00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:32.342
Suddenly an extraordinary sound came from the swamp!

82
00:04:33.043 --> 00:04:35.783
The dogs barked and the family jumped up in excitement.

83
00:04:36.523 --> 00:04:38.044
"That sounds like a bull bellowing!"

84
00:04:38.284 --> 00:04:38.644
I said.

85
00:04:39.324 --> 00:04:40.745
Jack rushed off toward the marsh.

86
00:04:40.765 --> 00:04:42.685
"Come back!"

87
00:04:42.945 --> 00:04:43.485
cried Mother.

88
00:04:43.505 --> 00:04:46.326
"Don't worry," said Fritz with a smile.

89
00:04:47.006 --> 00:04:49.427
Jack soon returned, lugging the wet bag.

90
00:04:49.447 --> 00:04:53.468
"They were supposed to grow as big as rabbits before you saw them.

91
00:04:54.188 --> 00:04:56.231
But I guess I'll have to show them to you now.

92
00:04:57.032 --> 00:04:59.055
Everyone, meet Grace and Beauty."

93
00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:03.160
He opened the bag and out hopped two immense bullfrogs.
